<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DHOGGUR_USE_DECIDE_SNUFFLING_FOR_A_JOB. The dhoggur's chemical swell. Owner 2026-10-16: "if you mess with it, it swells
  with violent chemical reactions that make it three times as big and spewing fire (firespit). Stays that way for 1/3 of
  a day, then it can't do it again for another day." Added and removed ONLY by RimMandrake.TheForge.RM_CompDhoggurSwell
  (Source/RM_ForgeDhoggurSwell.cs), which owns the timing; no Disappears comp here.
  - MeleeDamageFactor is set by RM_Hediff_DhoggurSwell.CurStage from the Mod Settings scale (shipped x3); body size and
    health scale x3 are Harmony postfixes on Pawn.BodySize / Pawn.HealthScale, keyed on the same comp.
  - <abilities>: vanilla HediffDef.abilities grants RM_FireSpit (src/RimMandrake/Cauldron/Defs/AbilityDefs/RM_FireSpit.xml,
    also the Zisska's) while the hediff stands; the comp gives the animal the ability tracker vanilla withholds from
    animals. A manhunter uses it through JobGiver_Manhunter -> JobGiver_AIFightEnemy.GetAbilityJob. Both defs ship in
    the same composed mod (mandrake.rm.biomes, Biomes.compose.json: Cauldron and TheForge are both wave 0), and a def
    cross-reference resolves after every def is loaded, so the Cauldron keeping ownership costs nothing here.
-->
<Defs>
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RM_DhoggurSwell</defName>
    <label>chemical swell</label>
    <description>A runaway chemical reaction under the hide: the creature has swollen to several times its size, its seams glow and smoke, and it spits burning fluid. It will burn itself out in a few hours, and cannot happen again for a day after.</description>
    <hediffClass>RimMandrake.TheForge.RM_Hediff_DhoggurSwell</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(1.0, 0.45, 0.15)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <abilities>
      <li>RM_FireSpit</li>
    </abilities>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <painFactor>0.5</painFactor>
        <statFactors>
          <MeleeDamageFactor>3</MeleeDamageFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>
</Defs>
